<h2>Update to doric-themes version 1.4.0</h2>

<h3>The new <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">doric-meadow</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">doric-mountain</code> themes</h3>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">doric-meadow</code> is a light theme with yellow and green colours, while
<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">doric-mountain</code> has a similar albeit dark palette. They expand the
collection of the Doric themes to cover even more styles and
preferences.</p>

<h3>Diff colours are refined</h3>

<p>I improved the inter-theme consistency of all colours that apply to
diffs, such as those shown in <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">diff-mode</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">ediff</code>, and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">magit</code> buffers.</p>

<p>Before, some themes were needlessly more subtle than others while
certain colours could be hard to discern in some situations. For
example, if the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">diff-hl</code> package was in use and the fringe was set to
a thin line.</p>

<p>Other packages also benefit from this review, such as my <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">pulsar</code> and
<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">lin</code>.</p>

<h3>Matching parentheses are distinct from the active region</h3>

<p>The highlight of matching parentheses produced by <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">show-paren-mode</code> is
now distinct from the active region. The same is true for the current
line, per <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">hl-line-mode</code>.</p>

<h3>The <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">doric-themes-define-theme</code> should not fail in certain cases</h3>

<p>I fixed an issue that was reported to me by Amin Bandali where the
<code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">doric-themes-define-theme</code> was failing to instantiate a theme in the
macroexpanded code.</p>

<h3>The <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">bg-accent</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">fg-accent</code> palette entries are renamed</h3>

<p>This is relevant for those who rely on <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">doric-themes-with-colors</code>. The
new names are <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">bg-accent-primary</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">fg-accent-primary</code>. The old
ones will not longer work.</p>
